ined     HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  the tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is  evaluated visually and reported as follows     Do not show overexpression  0 to 1   no minimal immunoreactivity or  incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells     Show moderate  2   overexpression  weak to moderate complete membrane  immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells     Show strong  3   overexpression  strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in    30  of tumor cells     These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by  the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not  been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The  FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this  laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision         Addendum  1 by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on Thursday  REMOVED_MONTH 18   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 04 12 59PM  By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final  Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed  or corrected the diagnoses                       ADDENDUM NOTE   REASON  2  RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION  FISH  FOR HER 2 NEU  GENE AMPLIFICATION    Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     HER 2 neu gene in tumor cells  REMOVED_DATE  Not Amplified    See note     Note  Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER 2 signals  111  to  chromosome 17 signals  100  in 60 tumor cell nuclei  A ratio of greater than  2 0 or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu gene amplification adjusted for  chromosome 17 polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis     The results at or near the cutoff point  ranging from REMOVED_DATE   2 2  should be  interpreted with caution  Equivocal Amplification   Reference  Journal of  Clinical Oncology 25 118 145   REMOVED_CASE_ID          Addendum  2 by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronicall