Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  03 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  03 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 19 38 CLINICAL DATA  Left modified radical mastectomy in a 45 year old female with a left breast mass which on mammogram was highly suggestive of carcinoma  FNA REMOVED_DATE showed isolated atypical cells  highly suggestive of carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL ADENOCARCINOMA  90    GRADE REMOVED_DATE  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED   REMOVED_DATE CM IN SIZE  AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  10    CRIBRIFORM AND SOLID TYPES  THE RESECTION MARGINS ARE NEGATIVE FOR CARCINOMA  2  TWENTY SEVEN OF TWENTY SEVEN LYMPH NODES ARE NEGATIVE  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 54                                                                                     HORMONE BINDING ASSAY Addendum     RESULTS OF HORMONE BINDING ASSAYS AS REPORTED BY DAVID T  MACLAUGHLIN  PhD   726  REMOVED_CASE_ID   estrogen receptor  Negative  progesterone receptor  Negative  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 18     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 unfixed breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 12 25 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  Left breast and axillary contents  is a 25 x 21 x 5cm left mastectomy specimen with attached axillary contents and a 23 x 8cm ellipse of skin containing unremarkable 1cm in diameter nipple  No lesions on the skin surface are identified  The deep surface is a thin unremarkable fibrous tissue overlying adipose tissue and is inked  Serial sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 6cm stellate firm white mass in the upper outer quadrant  5cm from the nipple and 2cm from the closest deep margin  A representative portion of the mass is frozen as frozen section  1 and saved frozen  Another piece is saved for estrogen receptors  The remainder of the breast tissue is predominantly adipose tissue with thin strands of fibrous tissue  No additional suspicious lesions are seen  The attached 7 x 5 x 2cm portion of axillary tail contains unremarkable lymph nodes up to 1 3cm in size  Section Code  A D  tumor  E  closest deep margin  F G  surrounding breast tissue  H M  lymph nodes  N  nipple  Resident  Daniel D  Koelliker  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  David Weissmann  M D  O R  Diagnosis by  Michael Pins  M D  O R  Consulting Pathologist s   Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD Lisa H  Lerner  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Herbert Charles Hoover Jr   M D  PART A  LEFT BREAST AND AXILLARY CONTENTS PART B  LEFT BREAST PART C  AXILLARY CONTENTS   report_end  , Not_reported.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  12 REMOVED_MONTH 03 ACCESSIONED ON  12 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 14 15 CLINICAL DATA  Invasive ductal carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA   SEE TABLE  1   DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEVERAL SCATTERED MICROSCOPIC FOCI  AGGREGATING TO LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM   SEE TABLE  1   METASTATIC CARCINOMA TO 6 OF 10 LYMPH NODES   SEE TABLE  2 AND SEE NOTE   HEALING BIOPSY SITE  NOTE  Keratin immunostains confirm metastatic carcinoma in the lymph nodes  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA Tumor size  Multiple scattered microscopic foci aggregating to  0 3cm  Grade  REMOVED_DATE Lymphatic vessel invasion  Present  Blood vessel invasion  Not identified  Margin of invasive carcinoma  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater  Location of ductal carcinoma in situ  Within and beyond the region of the mass  Grade of ductal carcinoma in situ  2  Margin of ductal carcinoma in situ  Ductal carcinoma in situ extends to less than 0 2cm from the posterior and inferior margins of the specimen in two foci  Stains for receptors  Requested on block B  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  2 AXILLARY LYMPH NODES Number of positive lymph nodes  6  Number of lymph nodes examined  10  Number of lymph nodes with metastases less than 0 2cm  4  Extracapsular extension  None  Other forms of axillary involvement  None  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 18 30                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block B   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  24 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 14 09 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast biopsy left axillary node dissection   is a 21 x 7 x 2 4cm lumpectomy specimen with attached axilla  There are three guide wires in the specimen and a long stitch marking the lateral and axillary lateral margin and axillary tail  short stitch demarcating the anterior margin  and a bow tie demarcating the superior margin  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior blue  posterior black  superior green  inferior yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal tan yellow adipose tissue with intermixed white fibrous tissue  and numerous palpable nodules ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm  The nodules are ill defined and in most cases not visually discrete from the surrounding adipose and fibrous tissue  However the largest mentioned nodule is tan pink to tan white and is adjacent to a curled surgical clip  This largest nodule is 0 5cm from the anterior margin  1 5cm from the posterior margin 2 5cm from the inferior margin  2 2cm from the superior margin  and greater than 3 0cm from both the medial and lateral margins  The surgical clip is removed and representative sections are submitted as follows  A  Dominant nodule to anterior margin adjacent to curled clip  B C  Additional sections of nodule to anterior margin  D  Nodule to posterior and inferior margins  E H  Additional sections range from medial to lateral including nodular areas in all sections  I  One axillary lymph node  1 5 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm    quadrasected  J  One axillary lymph node  1 5 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm    bisected  K  One axillary lymph node  1 0 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm    bisected  L  One axillary lymph node  1 2 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5   bisected  M  Four axillary lymph nodes  0 8 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm    whole  N  Two axillary lymph nodes  1 2 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE    whole  O  Axillary cyst  1 0 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9   quadrasected  P Y Additional breast tissue sections  Resident  STEWART M  KNOEPP  MD   Ph D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Kevin S  Hughes  M D  PART   BREAST LEFT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   LYMPH NODE LEFT A , Yes.
