Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  09 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  09 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 12 16 CLINICAL DATA  DCIS on previous core biopsy  Calcification on mammogram                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT  NEEDLE  1  MEDIAL   BIOPSY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  60    GRADE REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION AS MEASURED ON A GLASS SLIDE  PRESENT WITHIN REMOVED_DATE CM OF THE INKED SURFACE  WITH LYMPHATIC VESSEL INVASION  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  COMEDO AND CRIBRIFORM TYPES  40   WITH ASSOCIATED MICROCALCIFICATIONS  PRESENT IN NINE OF TEN BLOCKS AND PRESENT AT INKED SURFACE  3  MICROCALCIFICATIONS WITHIN LOBULES  4  SCLEROSING ADENOSIS WITH MICROCALCIFICATIONS  5  SCAR CONSISTENT WITH PREVIOUS BIOPSY SITE  6  THE INTRAOPERATIVE GROSS DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  BREAST  RIGHT  NEEDLE  2  LATERAL   BIOPSY  1  CELLULAR MUCINOUS CARCINOMA  INVASIVE  REMOVED_DATE CM  FOCALLY EXTENDING TO MARGIN  SEE NOTE   2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SOLID PAPILLARY TYPE  PRESENT IN THREE OF SEVEN BLOCKS  EXTENDING TO MARGIN  3  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  CRIBRIFORM TYPE  SEVERAL FOCI PRESENT IN THREE OF SEVEN BLOCKS  4  SEVERELY ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA WITH EXTENSIVE CALCIFICATION  5  SCLEROSING ADENOSIS WITH EXTENSIVE CALCIFICATION  6  CYSTS  NOTE  Blood vascular and lymphatic invasion is not seen  BREAST  RIGHT  SUPERIOR MARGIN   BIOPSY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  Andrea Flieder  MD Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 17 12                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT  SPECIMEN  1  MEDIAL   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  BREAST  RIGHT  SPECIMEN  2  LATREAL   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 14 19 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number in two container   Right breast biopsy  needle  1  medial  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm fragment of breast with localizing wires and X ray  Inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm firm gritty ill defined nodule which abuts inked resection margin  Lesion to small to freeze  Representative sections in A through J with nodule in A through E   Right biopsy  needle  2 lateral  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm fragment of breast with localizing wire and X ray  Inked and sectioned to reveal unremarkable breast parenchyma  submitted entirely in K through Q  Also received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit nuber  and  right breast biopsy  superior margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm fibroadipose tissue  dissected and submitted entirely in R and S  Resident  CHIN LEE WU  MD  PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  1   RIGHT BREAST  MEDIAL   LESION SUSPICIOUS FOR INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  BUT TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  GROSS DIAGNOSIS  2   RIGHT BREAST  LATERAL   NO LESION SUSPICIOUS FOR INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  PART A  RIGHT BREAST MASS  1 PART B  RIGHT BREAST MASS  2 PART C  RIGHT BREAST  BIOPSY  SUPERIOR MARGIN    report_end  , Yes.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  23 REMOVED_MONTH 99 ACCESSIONED ON  23 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 16 12 CLINICAL DATA  Local recurrence after lumpectomy and radiation in  REMOVED_CASE_ID                                                                                       FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF INVASIVE OR IN SITU TUMOR  ONE BENIGN LYMPH NODE  FROM LATERAL ASPECT  MINOR FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  WITH RARE MICROCALCIFICATIONS Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 13 57                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 7 0cm simple mastectomy specimen surfaced by an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 15 0cm tan skin ellipse  There is an undesignated short suture on one aspect  taken as superior  and an undesignated long suture at one tail end  taken as lateral   There is an eccentric unremarkable nipple areolar complex which abuts the inferior skin margin  Submitted additionally there is a 6 0cm in length linear  well healed scar located 11 5cm superolaterally from the nipple  The scar comes within 0 8cm of the closest lateral skin margin  Sectioning beneath the scar reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm centrally hemorrhagic biopsy which is outlined by a firm rim of indurated fibrotic parenchyma  The biopsy cavity is located 3 7cm from the closest deep margin  6 0cm from both the closest inferior and superior margins  8 5cm from the closest lateral margin  and 11 5cm from the closest medial margin  The remaining parenchyma is composed predominantly of unremarkable adipose tissue with scant areas of fibrous septae  No additional anomalies are noted  Section code  A C  representative sections of hemorrhagic biopsy cavity D  biopsy cavity in relation to overlying skin E  representative section of fibrous tissue from lateral side F  representative section of fibrous tissue from mid to central side G  representative section of single lymph node found in lateral aspect  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDAC                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  W B Jerry Younger  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Not_reported.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  22 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  22 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 18 53 CLINICAL DATA  63 year old female with biopsy proven right breast carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   PARTIAL MASTECTOMY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE 2 3  90   REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION  SEE NOTE  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  10   SINGLE FOCUS  COMEDO TYPE  3  BREAST ATROPHY  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA  EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 11 OF 11 LYMPH NODES  NOTE  Inked resection margins are free of carcinoma  the closest margin is at least 0 5cm  from tumor  There is no evidence of lymphatic or vascular invasion  Carcinoma is present in two of fifteen slides  Frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Leonard Atkins  M D  Signed On  27 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 13 57                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  30 AUG 95 at 15 14 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm fibroadipose tissue with wire in place and x ray demonstrating an ill defined stellate lesion  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 0 5cm firm gritty region with a central hemorrhagic cavity  This area is frozen as frozen section  1  and submitted in cassette A  Remaining tissue from that region is submitted in cassette B  Additional representative sections of tissue are submitted in cassettes C through O  Labeled  Axillary contents  is a piece of fibroadipose tissue  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm  Several lymph nodes are identified within this tissue  The largest lymph node is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm  The largest two are bisected and submitted entirely in cassettes P and Q  respectively  Remaining lymph nodes in R through T  Resident  Mark vanGorder  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  EDWIN S  MONUKI  MD O R  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Frederick William Ackroyd  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   PARTIAL MASTECTOMY PART B  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA  EXCISION   report_end  , No.
