Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  02 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  02 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 11 41 CLINICAL DATA  Breast mass with calcifications                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  90    REMOVED_DATE CM  GROSS MEASUREMENT   GRADE 3 OF 3  PRESENT REMOVED_DATE CM FROM A MARGIN  NEGATIVE FOR LYMPHATIC OR VASCULAR INVASION  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  10    HARBORING MICROCALCIFICATIONS  SOLID AND CRIBRIFORM TYPES  LOW GRADE  ADJACENT TO THE INVASIVE COMPONENT  2 OF 7 SLIDES   AWAY FROM MARGINS  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 19 45 Staff Pathologist  Dennis Sgroi  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 16 10     HER 2 Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR HER 2 c erb REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erb 2  See note  Note  This test was developed and its performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  It has not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 08 01 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm fibrofatty tissue fragment  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm ill defined stellate and firm mass which comes to 0 2cm to the closest resection margin  The remaining parenchyma is unremarkable with focal white fibrotic areas  The stellate mass is submitted in cassettes A and B  The remaining is submitted in toto in cassette C F  Gross Description by  QUN DONG  MD Resident  MELINDA J  FAN  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  HIGHLY SUSPICIOUS STELLATE AREA  0 7 X REMOVED_DATE CM  FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  QUN DONG  MD O R  Diagnosis by  ESTHER OLIVA  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  Peggy Lynn Ueda  M D  PART   B