rone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 13     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR C ERB  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  PROTEIN AS REPORTED BY IMPATH 1 800 447  REMOVED_CASE_ID  BREAST  RIGHT   30  OF THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR C ERB  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  PROTEIN  THE RESULT FALLS IN THE UNFAVORABLE CATEGORY  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 10 13 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm piece of breast which is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm firm  white to yellow nodule abutting the inked margin  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes A through E  with the nodule in A through C  Resident  CHIN LEE WU  MD  PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  SINGLE FIRM WHITE NODULE REMOVED_DATE CM IN DIAMETER  SUSPICIOUS BUT TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  STEPHEN LAU  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Eugene Jerome Mark  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT  MASS   report_end  , Yes.
